      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm seeing some weird issues on our subnet in lyon (193.253.x.x range). getting intermittent packet loss and some nasty jitter on the traceroutes. can u look at these ping stats and tell me if it looks like a physical layer issue or if something is wrong with the gateway?\n\nping 193.253.x.x:\n64 bytes from 193.253.x.1: icmp_seq=1 ttl=64 time=12.4 ms\n64 bytes from 193.253.x.1: icmp_seq=2 ttl=64 time=142.8 ms\n64 bytes from 193.253.x.1: icmp_seq=3 ttl=64 time=11.9 ms\n64 bytes from 193.253.x.1: icmp_seq=4 ttl=64 time=13.1 ms\nRequest timed out.\n64 bytes from 193.253.x.1: icmp_seq=6 ttl=64 time=155.2 ms\n\nthe spikes are really inconsistent.",
